e a recommended questions section, starting with the first question only. I'll make sure to note that the information is fetched from KLM, and it's essential to mention there's no emergency unless there are evident red flags. This will help keep things clear for the user without any panic. I'm focused on making my response well-structured and informative.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Current clinical picture**\nYou’re reporting **progressive exhaustion over the last few months**. From your stored record, I do see background **hypertension**, **chronic kidney disease stage 2**, prior elevated blood pressure readings, and kidney markers that may matter for fatigue context; your genomics also show variants associated with **hypertension/CKD risk**, but DNA alone does **not** explain day-to-day exhaustion.\n\n**Preliminary interpretation**\nAt this stage, your fatigue could be consistent with a few broad possibilities: **sleep-related causes**, **stress/overload**, **blood-pressure or medication-related effects**, or a **medical contributor** such as worsening kidney-related burden, anemia, thyroid issues, infection/inflammation, or other metabolic changes. The stored EHR/DNA context increases the importance of checking for a medical contributor, but your current symptom pattern still needs to be narrowed down.\n\n**Recommended questions**\nIf you answer a few focused questions, I can build a better preliminary picture before deciding whether the Doctor Agent should be involved.  \n**(1/5)** When did the exhaustion first start, and is it constant all day or worse at specific times (morning, afternoon, after activity)?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b1f2e0e9b82f35e0169d8f5206acc8191aa48ec579dce3e80\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":11073,"output":289,"cacheRead":12288,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23650,"cost":{"input":0.027682500000000002,"output":