that I need to ask a single question at a time from the Recommended Questions section. It seems like I should try to give the user one question to answer before moving on to the next. I want to avoid creating new questions while they're still answering the previous one. So, my plan is to focus on asking just the next question. That should keep things simple and clear for the user!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Recommended questions**\nThank you — that pattern suggests a subacute process over about a month, with symptoms building later in the day rather than being purely constant.\n\n**(2/5)** Has your exercise tolerance changed — for example, do stairs, walking, or routine activity feel noticeably harder than usual, or do you get short of breath, chest discomfort, palpitations, dizziness, or leg swelling with exertion?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b1f2e0e9b82f35e0169d8f579a1288191ba97b26a3a41c92c\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":11493,"output":142,"cacheRead":12160,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23795,"cost":{"input":0.0287325,"output":0.00213,"cacheRead":0.0030399999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0339025}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775826284772}}
