or cardiology record\n- Genomics/risk context: ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A; high PRS for hypertension and CKD progression\n\nCurrent symptom history from user:\n- Exhaustion worsening over ~1 month, worse in the evening\n- More tired even with small physical activity / reduced exercise tolerance\n- Shortness of breath and dizziness with exertion\n- Some fever\n- Black stools over the last month\n- Bad sleep\n- Unintentional weight loss\n\nHRV / smartwatch attachment summary:\n- Single uploaded series dated 2026-02-15 from 18:30 to 18:51 UTC\n- Values presented as bpm roughly ranging from ~51.3 to ~59.9, mostly mid-50s, no obvious extreme tachycardia in the sample\n- No formal HRV metrics provided (e.g. RMSSD/SDNN), just time-series pulse values\n\nTask:\nProvide a concise but clinically useful diagnostic assessment for the patient agent to relay directly to the user. Prioritize likely explanations and red flags. Address whether the HRV upload changes the assessment. Make clear if this pattern is concerning for GI bleeding/anemia versus cardiopulmonary or infectious/systemic causes. Keep it structured and patient-facing.","label":"doctor-agent-review","runtime":"subagent","mode":"run","cleanup":"delete","timeoutSeconds":120,"runTimeoutSeconds":120,"cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent"},"partialJson":"{\"task\":\"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent, providing specialized diagnostic support to the LoopAI Patient Agent. Review this case and return a patient-facing diagnostic assessment as-is, with clear uncertainty and safety-aware reasoning, but without sending the user elsewhere outside this system.\\n\\nPatient: PT-8839-CR\\nStored context from KLM/EHR/genomics:\\n- 48-year-old male\\n- Hypertension / uncontrolled hypertension\\n- CKD stage 2\\n- BP history includes 146/92 and 158/98\\n- eGFR declined from 82 to 71\\n- UACR increased from 45 to 135\\n- Medications: lisinopril increased to 20 mg, amlodipine 5 mg\\n- hs-CRP 5.2 mg/L, HR 88 bpm in prior cardiology record\\n- Genomics/risk context: ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A; high PRS for hypertension and CKD progression\\n\\nCurrent symptom history from user:\\n- Exhaustion worsening over ~1 month, worse in the evening\\n- More tired even with small physical activity / reduced exercise tolerance\\n- Shortness of breath and dizziness with exertion\\n- Some fever\\n- Black stools over the last month\\n- Bad sleep\\n- Unintentional weight loss\\n\\nHRV / smartwatch attachment summary:\\n- Single uploaded series dated 2026-02-15 from 18:30 to 18:51 UTC\\n- Values presented as bpm roughly ranging from ~51.3 to ~59.9, mostly mid-50s, no obvious extreme tachycardia in the sample\\n- No formal HRV metrics provided (e.g. RMSSD/SDNN), just time-series pulse values\\n\\nTask:\\nProvide a concise but clinically useful diagnostic assessment for the patient agent to relay directly to the user. Prioritize likely explanations and red flags. Address whether the HRV upload changes the assessment. Make clear if this pattern is concerning for GI bleeding/anemia versus cardiopulmonary or infectious/systemic causes. Keep it structured and patient-facing.\",\"label\":\"doctor-agent-review\",\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"cleanup\":\"delete\",\"timeoutSeconds\":120,\"runTimeoutSeconds\":120,\"cwd\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":164,"output":539,"cacheRead":30848,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":31551,"cost":{"input":0.00041000000000000005,"output":0.008085,"cacheRead":0.007711999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.016207}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775826475374}}
